  "research": {
    "area-3": {
      "text": "The Shops at Don Mills, a prominent lifestyle center, is a key commercial hub in this area, featuring retail, dining, and entertainment options.\n\nThis type of mixed-use development often attracts families and provides a built-in audience for a child-friendly café concept.\n\nThe presence of existing venues like Kitaya Japanese Takeout, Asian Legend, CoCo, Diwan, and Sorento Italian Kitchen within a short distance indicates an established commercial environment.\n\nThere are already successful play cafes in Toronto, such as Pinocchio Play Café in Lawrence Park and The Willow Play Cafe, demonstrating a demand for such concepts.\n\nToronto has seen an increase in demand for local shops and services as more people work from home, which could benefit a neighborhood-focused café.\n\nThe space would likely be classified as an \"assembly occupancy\" under the Ontario Building Code and Fire Code, necessitating sufficient exits, washrooms, and a fire safety plan.\n\nA change-of-use permit would probably be required, even if no construction is planned, as moving from a retail or warehouse use to an assembly use typically increases hazard.\n\nAdditionally, Toronto's zoning bylaws must permit a \"recreation use\" for an indoor playground.\n\nIf the café intends to allow parents to drop off children, it may be considered a child care center and would require a specific license.\n\nThe City of Toronto also licenses \"amusement establishments,\" and it would be necessary to confirm if this concept falls under that category.\n\nSecuring these permits and approvals can be a lengthy process, potentially taking several months.\n\nKitaya Japanese Takeout offers Japanese cuisine including sushi, sashimi, ramen, udon, and croffles, with prices for mains generally ranging.\n\nAsian Legend, a Chinese restaurant, is known for its dim sum, particularly soup dumplings, and a variety of traditional dishes like Peking Duck and stir-fries, with a casual atmosphere and wheelchair accessibility.\n\nCoCo Bubble Tea provides a range of bubble teas, smoothies, and slushes.\n\nDiwan, located within the Aga Khan Museum, offers Middle Eastern, North African, and South Asian cuisines with a seasonal menu and refined dining experience.\n\nSorento Italian Kitchen serves Italian dishes, including various pasta, wood oven pizzas, and entrees.\n\nThe Shops at Don Mills is a key feature of the area, designed as a \"lifestyle centre\" with a network of internal streets and on-site parking.\n\nIt is described as a mixed-use development with residential and retail spaces.\n\nThe area benefits from proximity to the Don Valley Parkway and public transit routes, enhancing accessibility.\n\nThe Aga Khan Museum is also nearby, which contributes to the cultural landscape.\n\nWhat to check on a visit\n\nA site visit should confirm the commercial zoning of specific properties and inquire about their suitability for a \"recreation use\" which is how an indoor playground is typically classified in Toronto.",
